# Classical Thermodynamics
#
# The canonical home for the laws, the state postulate, the potentials, Maxwell relations, and equations of state that engineering, chemistry, materials, and ecology cite.

#>physics_thermo_classical
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!physics
#:form #!ledger
#:level #!foundation
#:review #!adversarial_checked
#:valence #!bone

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Classical Thermodynamics"
 ~#claim: "Four laws, a state postulate, and a family of potentials decide what any process may do, before atoms enter the story."
 ~#proof: "Callen for the postulates and potentials, Gibbs for the phase rule, Carnot for the reservoir-only limit, Clausius 1850 and the 1854 Joule and Thomson absolute scale for its explicit form; each keystone links its source."
 ~#door: "Stretch a rubber band, then follow entropy into statistical mechanics."
 ~#audience: "students meeting thermodynamics in physics, chemistry, or engineering"
 continuity: "Classical Thermodynamics | four laws"
 cold_open: "Four laws and a handful of potentials decide what any engine, cell, or kitchen can do, and atoms never have to appear."
}

